{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Newly Constructed Multiple Dwellings Law rent control exemption","requirement":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings are exempt from any local rent control ordinance for 30 years following completion of construction. Government-subsidized rents may also be exempt from local rent control.","key_value":"30 years following completion of construction","coverage_conditions":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings in municipalities with rent control or rent leveling ordinances.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings"},"exemptions":"Rents subsidized by governmental funding may also be exempt from local rent control; HUD-subsidized or HUD-insured developments and NJHMFA-financed projects are not subject to municipal rent control ordinances.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.5","quoted_span":"Under the Newly Constructed Multiple Dwellings Law ( N.J.S.A. 2A:42 -84.5), newly constructed multiple dwellings shall be exempt from any local rent control ordinances for a period of 30 years following completion of construction of the building.","interaction":"New Jersey has no state rent control law; municipalities may adopt rent control ordinances, and this exemption limits those local ordinances.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act rent increase notice and unconscionability standard","requirement":"A landlord may not raise rent mid-lease: the old lease must be terminated and a new lease offered at the increased rent, with written notice, and the increase must not be unconscionable.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential tenants; applies to rent increases and to eviction for nonpayment of an increased rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"The increase in rent must not be unconscionable; it must not be so unreasonable as to shock the conscience of a fair and honest person and must comply with any municipal ordinances governing rent increases.","interaction":"A local rent control ordinance governs the allowable increase for covered units.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Conversion rent increase prohibition","requirement":"When a building is converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership, rents may not be increased to cover costs resulting solely from the conversion.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All tenants in a building converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership, whether or not eligible for protected tenancy.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Increases to cover the cost of new services or amenities are not prohibited.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.31","quoted_span":"If a building is converted to a condominium or cooperative form of ownership, or to fee simple ownership of units, rents may not be increased to cover cos ts resulting solely from the conversion (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.31).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act good cause requirement","requirement":"A residential landlord may evict or fail to renew a lease only for good cause and only through the legal process, after serving a written Notice to Quit describing each cause in detail, except for nonpayment of rent.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units used as a residence; no residential landlord may evict or fail to renew a lease, written or oral, without good cause.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rentals"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No residential landlord may evict or fail to renew a lease, whether it is a written or an oral lease without good cause. The landlord must be able to prove in court that he has grounds for an eviction.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit transfer and withholding penalties","requirement":"A new owner must obtain the tenant's deposit and accrued interest and is responsible for investing it, giving notices, paying interest and returning it. Willfully withholding a deposit of a tenant on government rental assistance carries a civil penalty of $500 to $2,000 per offense.","key_value":"$500-$2,000 per offense","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; special penalty protection for tenants receiving State or federal financial assistance, including welfare or rental assistance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Civil penalty of $500 to $2,000 per offense for willfully withholding deposits of tenants receiving government assistance; unlawful use of deposit monies is a disorderly persons offense with a fine of at least $200 or up to 30 days' imprisonment, or both.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Any landlord who willfully and intentionally withholds a security deposit made by or on behalf of a tenant who has received financial assistance through any Stat e or federal program, including welfare or rental assistance , may be penalized. The landlord may be liable for a civil penalty of not less than $500 or not more than $2,000 for each offense.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Law Against Discrimination source of lawful income protection","requirement":"A landlord or rental agency may not refuse to rent or discriminate in the rental of housing because of a renter's source of lawful income, along with the other classes the LAD protects.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All landlord-tenant relationships, except two-family owner-occupied dwellings, rooms in an owner- or resident-occupied single home, and single-sex or age-restricted housing as to familial status.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":null},"exemptions":"Two-family owner-occupied dwellings; rooms in an owner or resident-occupied single home; residences planned for and occupied by one sex and age-restricted housing, as to familial status.","penalty":"Landlords who violate the LAD are subject to substantial fines and penalties, up to $10,000 for a first offense.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 10:5-12","quoted_span":"requires equal treatment in the sale or rental of housing regardless of race, creed, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, marital status, civil union status, domestic partnership status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender  identity or expression, mental and physical disability, nationality, or source of lawful income.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
